			"Office.IRibbonControl": {"displayName":"IRibbonControl","members":[{"name":"Context","kind":"property","declaredType":"Object","access":"read-only","doc":{"summary":"Represents the active window containing the Ribbon user interface that triggers a callback procedure. Read-only.","params":[],"source":"external"}},{"name":"Id","kind":"property","declaredType":"String","access":"read-only","doc":{"summary":"Gets the ID of the control specified in the Ribbon XML markup customization file. Read-only.","params":[],"source":"external"}},{"name":"Tag","kind":"property","declaredType":"String","access":"read-only","doc":{"summary":"Used to store arbitrary strings and fetch them at runtime. Read-only.","params":[],"source":"external"}}],"doc":{"summary":"Represents the object passed into the callback procedure of a control in a ribbon or another user interface that can be customized by using Office Fluent ribbon extensibility.","remarks":"The IRibbonControl object contains the name (ID) of the control and the current Window object for the Ribbon UI control.","example":"public void ButtonOnAction(IRibbonControl control)\n{\n MessageBox.Show(\"Button clicked: \" + control.Id);\n}\n\npublic void ToggleButtonOnAction(IRibbonControl control, bool pressed)\n{\n...if (pressed)\n MessageBox.Show(\"ToggleButton was switched on.\");\n else\n MessageBox.Show(\"ToggleButton was switched off.\");\n}","params":[],"source":"external"}},
			"Office.IRibbonExtensibility": {"displayName":"IRibbonExtensibility","members":[{"name":"GetCustomUI","kind":"method","signature":"GetCustomUI(RibbonID As String) As String","doc":{"summary":"Loads the XML markup, either from an XML customization file or from XML markup embedded in the procedure, that customizes the Ribbon user interface.","params":[{"name":"RibbonID","text":"The ID for the RibbonX UI.","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}}],"doc":{"summary":"The interface through which the Ribbon user interface (UI) communicates with a COM add-in to customize the UI.","remarks":"The IRibbonExtensibility interface has a single method, GetCustomUI.","example":"public class Connect : Object, Extensibility.IDTExtensibility2, IRibbonExtensibility\n...\npublic string GetCustomUI(string RibbonID)\n{\n StreamReader customUIReader = new System.IO.StreamReader(\"C:\\\\RibbonXSampleCS\\\\customUI.xml\");\n string customUIData = customUIReader.ReadToEnd();\n return customUIData;\n}","params":[],"source":"external"}},
			"Office.IRibbonUI": {"displayName":"IRibbonUI","members":[{"name":"ActivateTab","kind":"method","signature":"ActivateTab(ControlID As String)","doc":{"summary":"Activates the specified custom tab. This method returns S_FALSE if there is no Ribbon or the Ribbon is collapsed.","params":[{"name":"ControlID","text":"Specifies the Id of the custom Ribbon tab to be activated.","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}},{"name":"ActivateTabMso","kind":"method","signature":"ActivateTabMso(ControlID As String)","doc":{"summary":"Activates the specified built-in tab.","params":[{"name":"ControlID","text":"Specifies the Id of the custom Ribbon tab to be activated.","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}},{"name":"ActivateTabQ","kind":"method","signature":"ActivateTabQ(ControlID As String, Namespace As String)","doc":{"summary":"Activates the specified custom tab on the Microsoft Office Fluent Ribbon UI. Uses the fully qualified name of the tab, which includes the ID and the namespace of the tab.","params":[{"name":"ControlID","text":"Specifies the Id of the custom Ribbon tab to be activated.","type":"String"},{"name":"Namespace","text":"Specifies the namespace of the tab element.","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}},{"name":"Invalidate","kind":"method","signature":"Invalidate()","doc":{"summary":"Invalidates the cached values for all of the controls of the Ribbon user interface.","params":[],"source":"external"}},{"name":"InvalidateControl","kind":"method","signature":"InvalidateControl(ControlID As String)","doc":{"summary":"Invalidates the cached value for a single control on the Ribbon user interface.","params":[{"name":"ControlID","text":"","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}},{"name":"InvalidateControlMso","kind":"method","signature":"InvalidateControlMso(ControlID As String)","doc":{"summary":"Used to invalidate a built-in control.","params":[{"name":"ControlID","text":"","type":"String"}],"source":"external"}}],"doc":{"summary":"The object that is returned by the onLoad procedure specified on the customUI tag. The object contains methods for invalidating control properties and for refreshing the user interface.","remarks":"You can customize the Ribbon user interface (UI) by using callback procedures in COM add-ins. When the host application starts, the onLoad callback procedure is called. The callback procedure then returns a IRibbonUI object pointing to the user interface (UI). Use that object to invoke the Invalidate, InvalidateControl, and Refresh methods.","example":"<customUI ... OnLoad=\"MyAddInInitialize\" ...>","params":[],"source":"external"}},
